.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NQSMSIGN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqsmsign ,
.Nm nqsmvrfy ,
.Nm nqsmenc ,
.Nm nqsmdec
.Nd S/MIME: signed and encrypted mail
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqsmsign "nqsalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen" "const uint8_t *cert" "size_t certlen" "const char *entity" "size_t n" "int detached" "int64_t at" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqsmvrfy "const char *mime" "size_t n" "const uint8_t *const *anc" "const size_t *anclen" "size_t nanc" "int64_t at" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen" "nqx5f *signer"
.Ft int
.Fn nqsmenc "const uint8_t *const *rcert" "const size_t *rcertlen" "size_t nr" "const char *entity" "size_t n" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqsmdec "nqkalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen" "const uint8_t *cert" "size_t certlen" "const char *mime" "size_t n" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions are those of
.Xr nqcmssign 3
as mail (S/MIME, RFC 8551).
The content is a MIME entity: its header lines and its body, such as
.Ql Content-Type: text/plain ,
an empty line, and the text.
Its line ends are made CRLF before it is signed or encrypted, as S/MIME
requires (RFC 8551 section 3.1.1): a lone CR or LF becomes CR LF.
An entity is at most 1 GiB
.Pq Dv NQELIM .
.Pp
.Fn nqsmsign
signs the entity: an
.Ql application/pkcs7-mime
entity of the smime-type
.Ql signed-data
with the content inside or, when
.Fa detached
is not 0, a
.Ql multipart/signed
entity whose first part is the content in the clear and whose second is
the signature, so that a mail reader without S/MIME still shows the
text.
Its
.Ql micalg
is that of the signature's digest
.Pq Ql sha-256 , sha-384 , sha-512 , shake128 No or Ql shake256 ,
as
.Xr nqcmssign 3
picks it), and its boundary is
.Ql ----noqtis-
and 32 hex digits from
.Xr nqrand 3 .
.Fn nqsmvrfy
checks either form as
.Fn nqcmsvrfy
does, and gives the signed entity.
.Pp
.Fn nqsmenc
encrypts the entity to ML-KEM certificates
.Po
.Ql application/pkcs7-mime ,
.Ql authEnveloped-data
.Pc ;
.Fn nqsmdec
opens it.
To sign and encrypt, sign first and encrypt the result.
.Pp
The results are text with CRLF line ends: the header fields
MIME-Version, Content-Type, Content-Transfer-Encoding and
Content-Disposition, an empty line, and base64 in lines of 64
characters; the parts are named
.Pa smime.p7m
and
.Pa smime.p7s .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Those of
.Xr nqcmssign 3 ;
.Dv NQEDEC
also for an entity that is not of these types.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sign a short text mail, detached:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static const char ent[] =
  "Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\en\en"
  "The results are in the capsule.\en";
static char out[1 << 16];
size_t n;
int rc = nqsmsign(NQMLDSA65, sk, sklen, cert, certlen, ent,
                  sizeof ent - 1, 1, (int64_t)time(NULL), out, sizeof out,
                  &n);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-smime 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqcmssign 3 ,
.Xr nqx5self 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%A J. Schaad
.%A B. Ramsdell
.%A S. Turner
.%T Secure/Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (S/MIME) Version 4.0 Message Specification
.%R RFC 8551
.%D April 2019
.Re
.Pp
RFC 9788 (August 2025) updates RFC 8551 with header protection, which is
not implemented: the code follows RFC 8551.
